S("TSiH9MUh4Ec","Phaser Drums - How to turn a Phaser into a Drum Synthesizer",
 "phaser-drums-ping-allpass-bank-short-impulse-feedback-ring-poles-sequenced-sweep-and-resonance",
 "Phaser drums: ping a phaser's all-pass filter bank with a very short impulse (a gate/trigger or just the attack of a sample), raise feedback/resonance until the bank rings like a tom, use more poles for complex liquid timbres, and sequence the sweep (centre frequency) and resonance per step to get tuned, accented percussion",
 "Turn any phaser into a resonant percussion voice. Delta vs phaser cluster (phaser pads, four-bar ramps, notch/comb movement, building a phaser from all-pass stages): here the phaser is the sound source, excited by impulses (filter pinging), not a modulation effect on a sustained pad.",
 ["Any phaser with feedback/resonance and pole-count controls (hardware or plugin)","A trigger/gate source or a sampler that can play only a very short attack slice","A step sequencer or MIDI clip with automation/modulation lanes"],
 [("impulse","audio","Very short click/gate or the first few ms of a sample",True),("pattern","midi/steps","Rhythm for the impulses",True),("pitch_steps","list","Per-step sweep/centre-frequency values (fixed, not random)",False)],
 [("phaser_percussion","audio","Liquid tom/bell-like tuned percussion from a ringing all-pass bank")],
 ["Start with phaser feedback low and output level down; high resonance can self-oscillate and jump in level, so keep a limiter on the track.","Per-step pitch values are fixed sequenced notes; no random sweep or wobble (Matt's preference).","Keep hits sparse, not rapid rolls or clicks; drums still enter early (~8 counts / ~12 s) if this is the main percussion.","Portable: any phaser with feedback and pole count; a trigger into an audio input on hardware equals a sampler playing a 1-5 ms attack slice in a DAW."],
 [("Set the phaser's LFO depth/rate to minimum so it doesn't sweep on its own; keep only the output up.","Phaser","Static all-pass bank"),
  ("Feed a very short impulse into the phaser: a gate/trigger pulse, or a sampler playing only the attack portion of any sample.","Trigger/sampler","A dry click comes through"),
  ("Raise feedback/resonance until the click rings with body.","Phaser feedback","Tom-like pitched ring after each hit"),
  ("Increase the pole/stage count (e.g. 4 to 8 to 12) for more complex, liquid timbres; try the phaser's alternative mode if it has one for a drummier tone.","Poles/mode","Richer, less oscillator-like ring"),
  ("Turn the sweep/centre frequency by hand to find the tuning range, then sequence it per step (automation or CV/mod lane) to play a melodic percussion line in key.","Sweep automation","Tuned percussion melody"),
  ("Sequence feedback/resonance per step too, so some hits ring longer as accents.","Resonance automation","Rhythmic variation through ring length"),
  ("Optionally modulate the phaser's internal LFO rate/amount slowly for evolving timbre, then add reverb.","LFO + reverb","Moving but still tuned percussion")],
 ["With the impulse alone the sound is a click; with feedback up it rings at a pitch set by the sweep.","Changing sweep per step changes the hit pitch to the sequenced notes.","Peak level stays under the limiter ceiling at maximum resonance."],
 ["phaser","allpass","filter-ping","percussion","drum-synthesis","resonance","sequencing"])

S("sNdpvcQqrP8","How to make Ambient Dub Techno like Rhythm & Sound in Ableton with free plugins",
 "ambient-dub-techno-kit-sub-50hz-crushed-kick-pitched-down-rim-clap-phaser-ghosts-hard-pan-dusty-hat-crushed-break-hp-2k",
 "Ambient dub-techno kit: a 909-style kick pitched to peak just below 50 Hz, heavily bit-crushed with the mids removed; a clap pitched down 2 semitones with low sustain and short decay (rim-shot feel) on the last beat of every second bar into a huge parallel reverb; ghost and shaker hits high-passed and run through phaser, delay and reverb, hard-panned left/right; a noisy hat as constant dust; a chopped break bit-crushed and high-passed to only above 2-3 kHz; drum bus saturated at 50% wet",
 "Build the soft, dark, dubby drum layer of an ambient dub-techno track, plus the chord, drone and bass that sit with it. Delta vs drum-groove cluster (filtered vibey drum bus, sparse ambient drums, organic downtempo groove) and the dub stab family in the filter cluster: this is a whole-kit recipe where every percussion part is bit-crushed, phasered and spread, and a sub-50 Hz dark kick replaces a clicky one.",
 ["A drum sampler, a bit-crusher, a phaser, delay and a large reverb, a saturator","A simple subtractive synth (saw + square)"],
 [("tempo_bpm","number","Dub-techno tempo",True),("key","string","Key, e.g. F# minor",True),("break_loop","audio","Optional funk/drum break to chop",False)],
 [("dub_kit","audio","Dark, spacious, moving drum layer"),("chords_drone_bass","midi/audio","Filtered chord stab, background m9 drone and square bass")],
 ["Steady pitch: the source used a flutter/wow plugin on the break and randomised velocity on the chord filter; both are dropped. Use hand-set velocities so the filter varies without randomness (Matt's preference).","Ghost hits are a few chosen samples placed by hand, not random hits; no rapid rolls or clicking.","Drums enter early (~8 counts / ~12 s)."],
 [("Kick: a 909-style kick pitched down until its peak sits just below 50 Hz; bit-crush it heavily and cut a lot of the mids.","Sampler + bit-crusher + EQ","Dark, soft, deep kick without a click"),
  ("Clap: a 909-style clap on the last beat of every second bar, pitched down 2 semitones, sustain down and decay short so it sounds like a rim shot; bit-crush it and send to a huge reverb on a parallel chain.","Sampler envelope + parallel reverb","Relaxed, distant backbeat"),
  ("Ghost hits: a few percussion samples placed by hand; high-pass the rumble, add phaser, delay and huge reverb, and pan them hard left and hard right.","HP + phaser + delay + reverb","Dubby, wide ghost layer"),
  ("Shaker: two hits from a shaker loop in a sampler, high-passed, phaser for constant movement, into the big reverb.","Sampler + phaser","Moving, spacey shuffle"),
  ("Dust: an old drum-machine hat that sounds like enveloped white noise, played as a constant background.","Sampler","Dusty noise bed"),
  ("Break: chop a funk break into a sampler, rearrange slices into a fairly regular beat, bit-crush it, add phaser and reverb, and EQ out everything below ~2-3 kHz so it only fills the top.","Slicer + crusher + EQ","Top-only break texture"),
  ("Drum bus: saturate heavily with dry/wet at 50%.","Saturator","Glued, warm kit"),
  ("Drone: an m9 chord (e.g. F#m9) on beat 1 of every second bar from a filtered saw + square, pushed back with chorus and reverb.","Synth + chorus + reverb","Background harmonic bed"),
  ("Bass: a filtered square wave with notes between the kicks; add a kick-keyed compressor so they never overlap.","Mono synth + sidechain comp","Clean kick/bass alternation"),
  ("Chords: saw + square an octave below, heavy low-pass with resonance, filter envelope with a little attack and decay under 1 s, velocity to filter (lower velocity = darker); bit-crush instead of distortion, cut lows and crusher highs, phaser, heavy compression so level stays even as the filter opens, then huge reverb; automate delay feedback across the track.","Synth + crusher + phaser + comp + reverb/delay","Moving dub chords"),
  ("Response melody: square + saw an octave higher with a slow LFO on the filter, answering the chords.","Synth + slow filter LFO","Call-and-response line")],
 ["Kick spectrum peak is just under 50 Hz with little 300 Hz-2 kHz content.","Clap occurs only on the last beat of every second bar.","Break track has almost no energy below ~2 kHz; drum bus saturator is 50% wet."],
 ["drums","dub-techno","ambient","kick","bit-crush","phaser","reverb","drum-bus","chords"])

S("q6TxzspNL9Q","Music Production Tips and Tricks - Making a Techno Reverb Kick",
 "reverb-rumble-kick-parallel-aux-ny-comp-release-between-16th-8th-drive-short-verb-ducked-by-kick-synced-lowpass",
 "Reverb/rumble kick: feed a kick into three parallel returns (New York compression with release between a 1/16 and 1/8 note at the tempo, a 100% wet drive, and a 100% wet short, high-cut reverb), duck the reverb return with a sidechain compressor keyed by the kick, then low-pass the tail with a tempo-synced LFO and finish with a low-end enhancer",
 "Make a kick with a dark sub 'rumble' tail between hits. Delta vs drum-synthesis cluster (synthesized kicks, dark short kick, hybrid hits): a processing chain that turns any existing kick into a kick-plus-rumble bed, built on parallel returns. For ambient use, keep the drive and reverb level low so the rumble works as a soft sub bed under pads.",
 ["A kick sample or synth kick","Three return/aux channels: compressor + EQ, distortion/drive, reverb + sidechain compressor + filter"],
 [("kick","audio/midi","Kick on a 4/4 pattern",True),("tempo_bpm","number","Track tempo (sets compressor release and LFO rate)",True)],
 [("rumble_kick","audio","Kick with a ducked, filtered reverb rumble between hits")],
 ["Release math: 1/16 note in ms = 15000 / BPM (125 BPM gives 120 ms); 1/8 = 30000 / BPM; set release between them.","Filter LFO is tempo-synced and periodic (square/stepped or sine), never random; no rapid stutter (Matt's preference).","Drums enter early (~8 counts / ~12 s)."],
 [("Program a 4/4 kick; lower velocity on the weak beats (~80) and the medium beat (~90). Pull the kick level down to leave headroom.","MIDI + velocity","Gentle accent pattern, headroom for parallel chains"),
  ("Return A: compressor (sidechain EQ letting only lows trigger), threshold low, high ratio for ~10 dB gain reduction, fast-ish attack that still lets the transient through, release between a 1/16 and 1/8 note. Add EQ low and high shelf boosts after it. Blend under the dry kick.","Parallel compressor + EQ","Fatter kick, dry transient kept"),
  ("Return B: a drive/distortion at 100% wet, amount low (below ~20%), letting lows through.","Drive","Grit added by blend, not insert"),
  ("Return C: reverb at 100% wet, small size, high cut on, decay turned up so it rattles.","Reverb","Low rumbling tail"),
  ("Put a compressor after the reverb with external sidechain from the kick; set release to control how long the rumble swells back between hits.","Sidechain comp","Rumble ducks on each kick and blooms in the gaps"),
  ("Add a low-pass filter after that to remove high frequencies; modulate cutoff with an LFO synced between 1/8 and 1/16, then optionally a slow LFO on cutoff with low depth for long-term movement.","Auto filter + LFO","Dark, pulsing rumble"),
  ("Optionally send some reverb into the drive return, then put a low-end enhancer/drum-bus device on the kick for sub weight with light drive.","Drum bus","Full sub kick + rumble")],
 ["Parallel compressor shows ~10 dB gain reduction with release within the 1/16-1/8 window.","Reverb return level dips on every kick hit (sidechain working).","Rumble has little content above the filter cutoff."],
 ["kick","rumble","reverb","parallel-compression","sidechain","techno","sub","drum-synthesis"])

S("NZJ9bvuyII4","How to Make Lazy Ambient Music in Session View",
 "looper-drone-clips-sine-utility-fade-overdub-clusters-faders-capped-0db-group-8s-verb-pingpong-resample-commit",
 "Looper drone clips: a plain sine into a gain/utility device, a long low-cut reverb at 70% wet and a one-bar looper; overdub single notes and clusters by easing the gain up and down, save each loop as a clip, build four chord-cluster clips, map one fader per clip (capped at 0 dB) to fade them in and out live through a group with an 8 s reverb, ping-pong delay, tape colour and glue compression, then commit by resampling",
 "Make ambient drone loops from one sine and perform them into a recording. Delta vs generative drone cluster (follow-action clip pools, probability loops, random modulators): nothing is random; the player builds four fixed cluster clips by hand with soft gain fades, and mixes them live with mapped faders, committing the result by resampling.",
 ["A DAW with clip/session view or a looper, a MIDI controller with knobs/faders","A sine synth, gain/utility, reverb, delay, tape-style saturation, glue compressor"],
 [("key_notes","list","Notes and clusters for each clip, e.g. G3+B2+A3+D4+E4",True),("clip_count","number","Number of drone clips (4 in the source)",False),("field_recording","audio","Optional field recording bed",False)],
 [("drone_clips","audio clips","Four one-bar loop clips of layered sine notes"),("performance","audio","Resampled live fade performance")],
 ["The source's re-pitch/tempo-knob trick changes pitch and is left out for steady pitch; keep clips in warp mode that preserves pitch (Matt's preference).","Fade notes in and out with the gain device so there are no clicks at loop points.","Beatless drone piece; if drums are added, they enter early (~8 counts / ~12 s).","Portable: any looper plus clip launcher, or record one-bar loops to audio clips manually."],
 [("Chain: sine synth -> gain/utility -> reverb (long decay, low cut, 70% wet) -> one-bar looper. Map the gain to a knob.","Device chain + MIDI map","Ready to capture soft notes"),
  ("Start the looper recording, hold a note and ease the gain up then down, then let the loop play.","Looper + gain knob","First layer with no hard attack"),
  ("Audition and overdub more notes in the same way, mixing low single notes, fifths (e.g. F1+C2) and close clusters (e.g. G3+Ab3+Bb3).","Looper overdub","Rich one-bar drone"),
  ("Drag the loop into a clip slot, clear the looper (same length) and build the next clip; make about four.","Clip slots","Four contrasting drone clips"),
  ("Put the clip tracks in a group; map one fader per track with the maximum capped at 0 dB.","Group + MIDI map","Each drone can be faded in alone"),
  ("On the group: reverb ~8 s decay, low cut, 50% wet; ping-pong delay unsynced, 50% wet, ~70% feedback; gentle tape colour with hum and noise low; glue compressor.","Group FX","Single shared space"),
  ("Add an optional field recording track.","Audio track","Natural bed"),
  ("Resample the group to a new audio track and record a live take while fading clips in and out; commit to it rather than editing afterwards.","Resampling","Finished ambient take")],
 ["Each clip contains several overdubbed notes with no click at the loop point.","Fader maps top out at 0 dB.","Final take is a single resampled audio file."],
 ["ambient","drone","looper","session-view","clip-launch","performance","resampling","sine"])
